[size=5][b][color=#F0A35E]BONFIRE[/color][/b][/size]
[i]Rest at the bonfire. Your progress is kept.[/i]

A free save manager for FromSoftware games. Quick save before a boss, quick load after you die, and keep named backups of the moments that matter.
One small .exe with nothing to install and nothing injected into the game.[/center]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F0A35E]◆ Features[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Quick save & quick load[/b]: press [b]S[/b] before a boss and [b]L[/b] after you die ([b]F5[/b] / [b]F9[/b] also work).
[*][b]Named backups[/b]: [b]Enter[/b] → [i]+ New backup[/i] → call it "Before Malenia" → done.
[*][b]Every load can be undone[/b]. Your current save is archived automatically before anything is restored, so a wrong keypress never costs you a run.
[*][b]Verified restores[/b]: every file is checked with SHA-256 before your save is touched. A damaged backup can never overwrite a good save.
[*][b]All-or-nothing[/b]: if the game holds the save file open, the restore is cancelled and your save stays exactly as it was.
[*][b]Finds your saves automatically[/b], including Bloodborne under shadPS4 in every region.
[*][b]Warns you when the game is running[/b].
[*]Backups are plain [b].zip[/b] files in [i]Documents\Bonfire[/i]. You can open them without Bonfire.
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rsxcore/Bonfire/main/nexus/images/1-main.png[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F0A35E]◆ Supported games[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Dark Souls: Prepare to Die Edition
[*]Dark Souls Remastered
[*]Dark Souls II / Scholar of the First Sin
[*]Dark Souls III
[*]Bloodborne (shadPS4)
[*]Sekiro: Shadows Die Twice
[*]Elden Ring
[*]Armored Core VI
[*]Elden Ring Nightreign
[/list]

Is your save somewhere else? Select the game and press [b]P[/b] to point Bonfire at the folder.

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F0A35E]◆ Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download and unzip [b]Bonfire.exe[/b] anywhere.
[*]Run it. It looks best in [b]Windows Terminal[/b], the default terminal on Windows 11.
[*]That's it: no installer, no mod manager, no game files touched.
[/list]

To uninstall, delete the exe. Your backups stay in [i]Documents\Bonfire[/i].

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F0A35E]◆ Controls[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]↑ ↓[/b]: move
[*][b]Enter[/b]: open a game, create a new backup, or restore the selected one
[*][b]S / F5[/b]: quick save (one slot per game, replaced each time)
[*][b]L / F9[/b]: quick load
[*][b]R[/b]: rename a backup, [b]D[/b]: delete one
[*][b]O[/b]: open the save folder, [b]B[/b]: open the backups folder
[*][b]P[/b]: set a custom save folder
[*][b]?[/b]: all keys
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F0A35E]◆ FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Is it safe to use online?[/b]
Bonfire only copies save files, the same thing you'd do by hand in Explorer. It never touches the game process, its memory or its files. As with any save backups, use them responsibly online.

[b]Can I load a backup while the game is running?[/b]
Go back to the title screen first, then load. Bonfire warns you if the game is running.

[b]My antivirus flags the exe.[/b]
Bonfire is open source and built automatically on GitHub from the public code. Unsigned tools are sometimes flagged by heuristics. You can check the source or build it yourself.

[b]Where are my backups?[/b]
In [i]Documents\Bonfire\<game>[/i]. Press [b]B[/b] in the app to open the folder. You can change it in settings ([b],[/b]).

